#
# HSET - single-field insert returns 1 (one new field).
#
1
Alice
#
# HSET - overwriting an existing field returns 0 (nothing new
# added), matching Redis semantics.
#
0
Alicia
#
# HSET - multi-field form returns the count of NEW fields added
# (not the total count of supplied pairs). Here 'name' is
# preexisting (counts 0), 'age' and 'city' are new -> returns 2.
#
2
#
# HGET - non-existent field returns nil.
#

#
# HGET - non-existent hash returns nil.
#

#
# HMGET - mix of existing and missing fields.
#
Alicia

30

Stockholm
#
# HMSET - legacy alias, returns +OK (per Redis spec - distinct
# reply shape from HSET's field-count).
#
OK
Bob
Oslo
#
# HDEL - single-field delete returns 1, repeat returns 0.
#
1
0

#
# HDEL - multi-field delete returns the count of fields that
# actually existed and were removed (missing fields do not count).
#
2
#
# Cleanup. Note: DEL only clears string_keys, so DEL on hash
# names returns 0 - a consequence of the namespace split (see
# rondis_namespace_split.test). HDEL by field is the only way
# to clear hash entries today.
#
0
